  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Marshall County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Marshall County | Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Marshall County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to the Marshall County Elections Website.\n The Auditor and Recorder's Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrimary Election Q&A\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nSep\n \n8\n \n \n\n West Marshall CSD PPEL Special\n Special Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan someone with a previous felony conviction vote?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nThose with a prior felony conviction are only permitted to vote if their voting rights have been restored by the Governor. For more information about restoration of rights, contact the Governor’s office or visit the voter registration page on our website. \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan a homeless person register to vote?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. Any eligible voter in Iowa may register to vote. Because many of those who are homeless have a nontraditional address they just need to provide an address or description of where they sleep the most, wherever that may be. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Marshall County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated January 21, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n8,187\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n8,069\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n6,455\n \n\n \nLibertarian\n \n\n\n \n155\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n42\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 22,908\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Marshall County, Iowa, Elections website at elections.marshallcountyia.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Auditor/Recorder Office\n\n 1 E. Main St.\n\n Marshalltown, Iowa 50158\n\n Phone: (641) 754-6323\n\n Fax: (641) 844-2727\n\n Hours: M-F 8:00 to 4:30\n \n \nElection Center\n\n 107 S. 1st Ave.\n\n Marshalltown, IA 50158\n\n Phone: (641) 754-6302\n\n Hours: M-F 8:00 to 4:30\n\n Open for Business Twenty (20) Days Prior to Election Day\n \n \nMailing Address\n\n for the Auditor/Recorder and Elections\n\n 1 E. Main St.\n\n Marshalltown, IA 50158\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n \nContact Us •\n Accessibility •\n Marshall County Website\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
